{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1444","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Finding the Vertex"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This is an interactive problem."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a tree — connected undirected graph without cycles. One vertex of the tree is special, and you have to find which one. You can ask questions in the following form: given an edge of the tree, which endpoint is closer to the special vertex, meaning which endpoint's shortest path to the special vertex contains fewer edges. You have to find the special vertex by asking the minimum number of questions in the worst case for a given tree."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Please note that the special vertex might not be fixed by the interactor in advance: it might change the vertex to any other one, with the requirement of being consistent with the previously given answers."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 100$$$) — the number of vertices in a tree."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The folloiwing $$$n-1$$$ lines contain two integers each, $$$u$$$ and $$$v$$$ ($$$1 \\le u, v \\le n$$$), that denote an edge in the tree connecting $$$u$$$ and $$$v$$$. It is guaranteed that the given edges form a tree."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"custom","title":"Interaction"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Interaction"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After reading the input data, one can start making queries. There are two possible queries:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"? $$$u$$$ $$$v$$$"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" — to ask for an edge $$$(u, v)$$$ ($$$1 \\le u, v \\le n$$$) which of the endpoints is closer to the special vertex. The answer to this query is one of the endpoints. Note that, $$$u$$$ and $$$v$$$ must be connected by an edge, and hence they can not have the same distance to the special vertex."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"! $$$u$$$"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" — to indicate that you found the special vertex. After the program does that, it must immediately terminate. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Do not forget to output the end of line and flush the output. Otherwise you will get "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Idleness limit exceeded"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" verdict. To flush the output, you can use: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fflush(stdout)"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cout.flush()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C++"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"System.out.flush()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Java"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"flush(output)"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Pascal"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"sys.stdout.flush()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Python"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" see documentation for other languages. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In case you ask more queries than needed in the worst case for a given tree, you will get verdict "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Wrong answer"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n1 2\n2 3\n3 4\n4 5\n3\n2\n1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n? 3 4\n? 2 3\n? 1 2\n! 1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n2 1\n3 1\n4 1\n5 1\n1\n1\n4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n? 1 2\n? 1 3\n? 1 4\n! 4\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Hacks are forbidden in this task."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"1444E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1444/problem/E"}